      "id": "P1",
      "text": "COLONOSCOPY REPORT"
    },
    {
      "id": "P2",
      "text": "Date of service: November 5, 2026"
    },
    {
      "id": "P3",
      "text": "Endoscopist: Desmond Achebe-Rowe, MD (fictional)"
    },
    {
      "id": "P4",
      "text": "Procedure: The colonoscope was advanced to the cecum, confirmed by the appendiceal orifice."
    },
    {
      "id": "P5",
      "text": "- Descending colon: a 6 mm sessile polyp, removed completely with a cold snare and retrieved."
    },
    {
      "id": "P6",
      "text": "- Hepatic flexure: a 10 mm sessile polyp on the proximal side of a thick fold."
    },
    {
      "id": "P7",
      "text": "- Snare removal of this polyp was attempted, but the snare could not be positioned around it."
    },
    {
      "id": "P8",
      "text": "- The hepatic flexure polyp was not removed, and no tissue was taken from it."
    },
    {
      "id": "P9",
      "text": "1. 6 mm descending colon polyp, removed by cold snare."
    },
    {
      "id": "P10",
      "text": "2. 10 mm hepatic flexure polyp, not removed after a failed snare attempt."
    },
    {
      "id": "P11",
      "text": "Plan: Repeat colonoscopy with a distal cap in 4 to 6 weeks to remove the hepatic flexure polyp."
    }
  ],
